course: dictionary
lesson: 5704
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words change meaning depending on where you are. The word lolly is a good example. In the UK and Ireland, a lolly is an ice lolly, which is frozen juice on a stick, or a lollipop, which is a hard sweet on a stick. «Harry also took a pound from Mum's purse for a lolly.» Here the pound tells you a lolly is something you buy, so it means a sweet.
explain: In Australia and New Zealand, a lolly is any sweet or candy. A friend there might say, «The lolly aisle is busy today», and she means the sweets section of the shop. Always check the clues around the word, and check where the speaker lives if you can.
explain: In British slang, lolly means money. So if someone asks, «Can you lend me a lolly?», they want money, not a sweet. Ask yourself: does this sentence make sense with my meaning swapped in?
fact: Lolly means different things in different places, so check the context.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, «lolly» means an ice lolly or a lollipop.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «lolly» means any sweet or candy.
fact: In British slang, «lolly» means money.
fact: A «lollipop lady» in the UK helps children cross the road, using a round sign.
exercise: «Harry also took a pound from Mum's purse for a lolly.» What is a lolly in this sentence? | *A sweet you buy | A park bench | A coin | A bus ticket
exercise: In Australia, a friend says, «The lolly aisle is busy today.» Where is she? | At the swimming pool | At the bus stop | *In the sweets section of the shop | In the bank
exercise: What does a lollipop lady do? | Counts money at the bank | *Helps children cross the road | Bakes cakes for parties | Sells ice lollies at the beach
test: «Mrs Lee bought the park kids ice lollies with her bingo money.» What is an ice lolly? | A pound coin | A bingo card | *Frozen juice on a stick | A park bench
test: A friend in London says, «Can you lend me a lolly until Friday?» What does lolly mean? | A sweet on a stick | A cold drink | *Money | A ticket for the bus
exam: «Wet skin can freeze and stick to a very cold ice lolly.» What can happen if wet skin sticks to a frozen lolly? | It makes the lolly bigger | *It can tear when you pull away | It melts at once | It turns into a sweet
